# CraftCanvas Implementation Plan - UI/UX Audit and Enhancements

This plan outlines the steps to visually audit the CraftCanvas frontend, identify areas for improvement in aesthetics and structure, and implement a more premium, dynamic user interface.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> I will be performing a visual audit using the browser tool. I will propose specific UI/UX changes after the audit.
> Significant restructuring of the dashboard or main navigation will be presented for approval before implementation.

## Proposed Changes

### [Phase 1: Visual Audit & Research]
- Capture screenshots of the current dashboard, login, and key module pages (Tasks, Courses, etc.).
- Analyze the [globals.css](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/app/globals.css) and existing components to understand the current design system.
- Research modern "Glassmorphism" and "Academic Productivity" aesthetics for inspiration.

### [Phase 2: Core Design System Update]
- **[MODIFY] [globals.css](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/app/globals.css)**
  - Refine color palette with more "premium" HSL-based colors.
  - Enhance glassmorphism utility classes (blur, border-opacity, background-saturation).
  - Standardize typography and spacing tokens.
- **[MODIFY] [tailwind.config.ts](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/tailwind.config.ts)**
  - Ensure modern Tailwind 4 features are leveraged if applicable.

### [Phase 3: Component Enhancements]
- **[MODIFY] [Logo.tsx](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/components/Logo.tsx)**
  - Ensure the pixel art logo is sharp and fits the premium aesthetic.
- **[MODIFY] Navigation/Sidebar Components**
  - Add micro-animations (Framer Motion) for hover and active states.
  - Implement a more refined, less "boxy" layout.

### [Phase 4: Dashboard Restructuring]
- **[MODIFY] [page.tsx](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/app/page.tsx)**
  - Optimize the "Module Hub" for high-density information without feeling cluttered.
  - Use 2-column grids and hover-to-reveal actions as previously requested.
  - Increase vertical utilization of the screen.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Run existing Playwright E2E tests: `npx playwright test`.
- Check for accessibility (aria-labels, contrast) using browser audit tools.

### Manual Verification
- Visual inspection of all screens in the browser subagent.
- Verify "Wow factor" - does it feel premium and alive?
- Check responsiveness on different viewport sizes.
